From: CoreRouter <noreply@corerouter>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] tests: ospfd with many interfaces configured in a batch

r1 has 300 dummy interfaces with "ip ospf area 0", configured by the
"vtysh -f" that loads frr.conf. Check that each stub route of r1 is
directly attached to the interface that owns the prefix (the interface of
a router-LSA link is found by its position, ospf_if_lookup_by_lsa_pos()),
that the router-LSA has all the links and that r2 learns every prefix;
then the same after a batch takes OSPF off 100 of the interfaces (the
positions of the links that remain change) and another puts it back,
neither of them originating one router-LSA instance per interface.

Without "ospfd: one router-LSA per configuration batch", the last check
fails: each of those batches takes the sequence number 100 further.
